funcbound_cutoff_i386 -- the exact sectionless i386 witness for the
`funcboundflow` effective-cutoff branch-stub regression.

What it is
  A 5,208-byte statically linked, stripped ELF32 executable with no section
  table. The callback at 0x8048820 skips an embedded report string on its real
  path. Decoding the string as the conditional branch's other path produces a
  branch at 0x8048845 to 0x80488bc, the middle of the real instruction at
  0x80488bb; that reinterpretation branches again to the p-code-free bytes at
  0x80488de. Aggressive analysis discovers foreign entries in this region; the
  current default flow admits the shared return at 0x80488a5 and establishes a
  `funcboundflow` cutoff at 0x80488e0.

Why it is vendored rather than rebuilt
  The absence of a section table and the exact overlapping instruction streams
  are both load-bearing. Keeping the 5 KB witness byte-identical makes the
  promoted CLI acceptance exercise the same loader, discovery, and flow paths
  as the filed failure without requiring the external RE dataset in CI.

Where it came from
  The RE-friction loop's round-10 witness: challenge
  5ab77f5c33c5d40ad448c615 in the kuna-re-dataset crackme corpus ("trace_p by
  taviso", https://crackmes.one/crackme/5ab77f5c33c5d40ad448c615),
  `bin/trace-p.zip.__x/crackme`, byte-identical.

  sha256 7b8a32c3cc0e9816bfe03d2e7c4aa5a596a21e43a6e35dc43cb17fa5867138ec
  It is a third-party CTF-style crackme, included unmodified as test data only.
